From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree: GetHashFromBlob/Handle/File/AssemblyFile

The legacy shim hash entry points were stubs. They hash with the given
CryptoAPI algorithm (SHA-1 when 0, reported back), return the needed size
with ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER when the buffer is small, and read files
from the start.

Gate: test/mscoree-hash-gate.sh (64 and 32 bit; published digests of
"abc"). Mutants SG_MUTANT_HASH_DEFAULT, _SIZE and _FILE are caught.
---
--- a/dlls/mscoree/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/mscoree/Makefile.in
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@ SOURCES = \
 	metahost.c \
 	mscoree_classes.idl \
 	mscoree_main.c \
+	shimhash.c \
 	strongname.c
 
 metahost_EXTRADEFS = -DINSTALL_DATADIR="\"${datadir}\""
--- a/dlls/mscoree/mscoree.spec
+++ b/dlls/mscoree/mscoree.spec
@@ -45,12 +45,12 @@
 @ stdcall GetCORVersion(ptr long ptr)
 @ stub GetCompileInfo
 @ stdcall GetFileVersion(wstr ptr long ptr)
-@ stub GetHashFromAssemblyFile
-@ stub GetHashFromAssemblyFileW
-@ stub GetHashFromBlob
-@ stub GetHashFromFile
-@ stub GetHashFromFileW
-@ stub GetHashFromHandle
+@ stdcall GetHashFromAssemblyFile(str ptr ptr long ptr)
+@ stdcall GetHashFromAssemblyFileW(wstr ptr ptr long ptr)
+@ stdcall GetHashFromBlob(ptr long ptr ptr long ptr)
+@ stdcall GetHashFromFile(str ptr ptr long ptr)
+@ stdcall GetHashFromFileW(wstr ptr ptr long ptr)
+@ stdcall GetHashFromHandle(long ptr ptr long ptr)
 @ stub GetHostConfigurationFile
 @ stub GetMetaDataInternalInterface
 @ stub GetMetaDataInternalInterfaceFromPublic
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/mscoree/shimhash.c
@@ -0,0 +1,162 @@
